# Everything uses LF line endings in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Published files and their checksums are stored byte for byte. Without
# this, Git on Windows can convert line endings in a published text file
# on checkout, and its SHA512 checksum would no longer verify. These lines
# must stay below the one above, because later lines take precedence.
docs/*/v*/** -text
docs/*/corrections/** -text
